I found that the staff list is currently readable by every administrator-role account, even though only the configured super admin can change accounts. I’ll tighten both the API and the navigation; for email, I’m proposing durable, structured copy overrides for every automated email, while keeping HTML, links, and expiry rules controlled by the app.
{"kind":"tool","id":"fxt1_JDOHwo","toolName":"write_todos","input":{"todos":[{"task":"Explore the existing staff authorization, email flows, and project conventions","completed":true},{"task":"Clarify template scope, editable fields, and who may edit","completed":true},{"task":"Present and get approval for an implementation design","completed":false},{"task":"Write and self-review the approved design document","completed":false},{"task":"Get user review of the design document","completed":false},{"task":"Create the implementation plan from the approved design","completed":false}]}}
The current staff page lets every `admin`-role account read the staff list; only the super-admin check protects changes. Email content is currently hard-coded in the shared email sender, while the project already has a Postgres-backed database and administrator-only API patterns.

I’m interpreting your access request as: **only the configured super admin may view the staff list; other admin-role accounts must be denied by both the API and the interface.** For email templates, you chose all transactional emails, with editable copy but code-controlled HTML layout and security-sensitive links/expiry behavior; any `admin`-role account may edit them.### Approaches

1. **Structured copy saved in the database — recommended.** Admins edit defined text fields for each transactional email. The existing branded layout remains in code, which keeps the messages consistent and avoids letting editable HTML affect email safety.
2. **Full HTML editing.** More flexibility, but makes it easier to break layouts or introduce unsafe markup.
3. **Keep copy in code.** Simplest technically, but would not let admins edit templates through the panel.

### Proposed design

Add an **Email templates** area to the admin panel. Admin-role accounts can edit the subject, preheader, heading, message copy, action label, and general notes for the site’s transactional email types. Changes are saved to the existing database; if no override exists, the current built-in copy is used. The same saved copy feeds both HTML and plain-text versions.

The email layout, generated links, expiry rules, and other security-sensitive behavior remain code-controlled. The API will enforce the admin-role check as well as the interface.

For staff accounts, restrict both the staff-list API and the panel page to the configured super admin. Other admin-role accounts will not receive or see the staff list.

**Does this design look right to you?**

Got it — I’ll include adding links and let admins adjust button color and style, while keeping security-critical link destinations locked. I’m updating the mockup so you can see those controls before we finalize the design.
